### Page 1 of 2

```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Mayor Patrick Collins, and City Council
FROM:

TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager
DATE:

April 19, 2021
SUBJECT:
Consideration of Bid #E-22-21 for furnishing One (1) ¾ Ton Crew Cab Truck for
the Traffic Division, One (1) ¾ Ton Regular Cab Truck for the Facilities
Maintenance Division, and Three (3) ¾ Ton Crew Cab Trucks for the Street and
Alley Division.
______________________________________________
Three (3) bidders responded to this bid, and the bid tabulation is attached.

The Three (3) Bids were received from:
1. Rocky Mountain Yeti.  Afton, Wyoming.

2. Greiner Ford.  Casper, Wyoming.
a. (BID NOT IN COMPLIANCE, HOWEVER, NOT LOW BIDDER)

3. Spradley Barr Motors.  Cheyenne, Wyoming.

The bids were reviewed Vicki Nemecek (Public Works), Craig LaVoy (Public Works), Dennis
Fanning (Traffic), Steve Gaer (Facilities), Randy Hickman (Street & Alley), and Bryan Bell (Fleet
Maintenance).
Their recommendation is to accept the lowest responsive bid from Rocky Mountain Yeti, for the
purchase of One (1) ¾ Ton Crew Cab Truck for the Traffic Division, One (1) ¾ Ton Regular Cab
Truck for the Facilities Maintenance Division, and Three (3) ¾ Ton Crew Cab Trucks for the Street
and Alley Division, for a bid award amount of $222,437.00.

Funding:
022-26-2617-42-43201 (1% Sales Tax 15-18 / Motor Vehicles / Traffic)

Traffic $35,922.00
022-26-2615-40-43102 (1% Sales Tax 15-18 / Equipment / Facilities)
Facilities $33,581.00
022-26-2616-42-43102 (1% Sales Tax 15-18 / Equipment / Street & Alley)
Street & Alley $152,934.00
Total  $222,437.00
```

